body:
`export { HttpMethod }` only re-exports the runtime Zod schema value. If the intent is to let downstream consumers also import `type HttpMethod` from `@objectstack/spec/api`, you also need a type-only re-export (otherwise only `@objectstack/spec/shared` exposes the type).
```suggestion
export { HttpMethod };
export type { HttpMethod } from '../shared/http.zod';
```

The TypeScript snippet imports `HttpMethodSchema` from `@objectstack/spec/api`, but the API package exports `HttpMethod` (from `shared/http.zod.ts` via `api/router.zod.ts`), not `HttpMethodSchema`. As written, this example will not compile / will confuse consumers.
```suggestion
import { HttpMethod } from '@objectstack/spec/api';

// Validate data
const result = HttpMethod.parse(data);
```
